{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecificLimits.Normed","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Log","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Analytic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Analytic.OfScalars","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Analytic.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Analytic.ChangeOrigin","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.DominatedConvergence","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Integrals.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.LogBounds"],"declarations":30,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoExt_one_im","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoExt_one_im","kind":"theorem","line":606,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L606-L628","doc":"**`Li₂(1)` is real.** `cLiTwoExt_conj` cannot reach `y = 1` — it is on the\naxis, where the conjugation identity is exactly what fails in general — so this\nis proved the same way but from the *stronger* local fact: on `[0,1]` the\nintegrand `log(1 − z)/z` is real-valued outright, because `1 − z ≥ 0` there.\n\nStated as `.im = 0` rather than `= π²/6`: that is all the `5₂` bridge's `hone`\nhypothesis needs, and it avoids importing an evaluation this file does not\nprove. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoExt_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoExt_conj","kind":"theorem","line":577,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L577-L604","doc":"**`Li₂(ȳ) = conj (Li₂ y)` off the real axis.** See the section docstring for\nwhy `y.im ≠ 0` is required rather than merely convenient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.intervalIntegral_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.intervalIntegral_conj","kind":"theorem","line":570,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L570-L575","doc":"Conjugation passes through an interval integral, with **no integrability\nhypothesis**: `conj` is a linear isometry, so where `f` fails to be integrable\nso does `conj ∘ f`, and both sides are Bochner's junk value `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.intervalIntegrable_log_one_sub_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.intervalIntegrable_log_one_sub_div","kind":"theorem","line":540,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L540-L549","doc":"The original right-half-plane form, now a corollary. `Re(1 − yz) > 0` is\n**sufficient but not necessary** — it excludes most of `ℂ ∖ [1,∞)`, e.g.\n`y = 1.5 + 0.3i`. See `QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmSlit.lean` for the sharp\nhypothesis. Kept because `FiveTwoSumRuleIntegrand` documents this name. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.intervalIntegrable_log_one_sub_div_of_slitPlane","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.intervalIntegrable_log_one_sub_div_of_slitPlane","kind":"theorem","line":487,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L487-L538","doc":"**The `cLiTwoExt` integrand is interval-integrable on `[0,1]`** when\n`1 − yz` stays in the open right half-plane there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoExt_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoExt_zero","kind":"theorem","line":471,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L471-L472","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoExt_eq_cLiTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoExt_eq_cLiTwo","kind":"theorem","line":467,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L467-L469","doc":"On the open unit disc the integral definition and the series agree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoExt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoExt","kind":"def","line":458,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L458-L465","doc":"The dilogarithm by its integral definition, valid past the unit disc.\n\n    `Li₂(y) = −∫₀¹ log(1 − yz)/z dz`\n\nJunk-valued (`0`) where the integrand fails to be integrable, per Mathlib's\nconvention; every lemma about it carries the relevant hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo_eq_intervalIntegral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo_eq_intervalIntegral","kind":"theorem","line":340,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L340-L431","doc":"**The integral representation on the open unit disc.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.log_mul_log_one_sub_analyticOnNhd_ball_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.log_mul_log_one_sub_analyticOnNhd_ball_half","kind":"theorem","line":311,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L311-L318","doc":"The `log`-product term. Uses `mem_slitPlane_of_mem_ball_half` on both\nfactors — this is where `Re z > 0` earns its keep. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo_one_sub_analyticOnNhd_ball_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo_one_sub_analyticOnNhd_ball_half","kind":"theorem","line":302,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L302-L309","doc":"The reflected summand. Uses `one_sub_mem_ball_half` — this is where the\nself-mapping of the ball under `z ↦ 1−z` earns its keep. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo_analyticOnNhd_ball_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo_analyticOnNhd_ball_half","kind":"theorem","line":298,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L298-L300","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo_analyticAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo_analyticAt","kind":"theorem","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L291-L296","doc":"`cLiTwo` is analytic at each point of the open unit disc. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.mem_slitPlane_of_mem_ball_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.mem_slitPlane_of_mem_ball_half","kind":"theorem","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L279-L282","doc":"`ball(½,½) ⊆ slitPlane` — immediate from `Re z > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.re_pos_of_mem_ball_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.re_pos_of_mem_ball_half","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L267-L277","doc":"`Re z > 0` on `ball(½,½)`, so `log z` and `log (1−z)` avoid the branch cut. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.one_sub_mem_ball_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.one_sub_mem_ball_half","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L258-L265","doc":"`z ↦ 1 − z` maps `ball(½,½)` to itself, so `cLiTwo (1−z)` is fine too. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.norm_lt_one_of_mem_ball_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.norm_lt_one_of_mem_ball_half","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L249-L256","doc":"`ball(½,½) ⊆ ball(0,1)`, so `cLiTwo` is given by its series there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo_analyticOnNhd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo_analyticOnNhd","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L225-L235","doc":"**`cLiTwo` is analytic on the open unit disc.**\n\nThe hypothesis the identity theorem needs. With\n`QOU.Archimedean.cLiTwo_reflection_ofReal` (the reflection identity already\nproved on the real segment `(0,1)` — a set with an accumulation point), this is\nwhat would give the complex reflection identity on the disc. That continuation\nstep is **not** taken here; extending past `|z| = 1` needs the inversion\nformula on top. Bean `qou-gkco`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo_hasFPowerSeriesOnBall","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo_hasFPowerSeriesOnBall","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L206-L223","doc":"**Step 3: `cLiTwo` is represented by its power series on the unit ball.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo_radius_ge_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo_radius_ge_one","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L189-L204","doc":"**Step 2 of the analyticity route (bean `qou-gkco`): radius `≥ 1`.**\n\nImmediate from `cLiTwoCoeff_norm_le_one` via `le_radius_of_bound` at `r = 1`,\nwith no ratio test needed. Combined with `cLiTwo_eq_tsum_coeff`, this says the\ndefining series of `cLiTwo` is a genuine power series on the open unit disc.\n\nStep 3 — upgrading this to `AnalyticOnNhd ℂ cLiTwo (Metric.ball 0 1)`, which\nis what the identity theorem needs — is **not** done here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoCoeff_norm_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoCoeff_norm_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L179-L187","doc":"Every coefficient has norm `≤ 1`: `c₀ = 0` and `‖1/n²‖ = 1/n² ≤ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo_eq_tsum_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo_eq_tsum_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L170-L177","doc":"**The two indexings agree.** `cLiTwo z = ∑' n, cₙ zⁿ` with `c` as above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoCoeff_summable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoCoeff_summable","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L151-L168","doc":"The standard-indexed series is summable on the open unit disc. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoCoeff_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoCoeff_succ","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L145-L149","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoCoeff_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoCoeff_zero","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L143-L143","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoCoeff","kind":"def","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L140-L141","doc":"The coefficients of `Li₂` in standard indexing: `c₀ = 0`, `cₙ = 1/n²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo_summable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo_summable","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L119-L126","doc":"The defining series converges on the open unit disc. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo_term_norm_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo_term_norm_le","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L107-L117","doc":"Each term is dominated by `‖z‖^(k+1)`, since `1/(k+1)² ≤ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo_zero","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L103-L105","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithm.lean#L93-L101","doc":"The complex dilogarithm as its defining power series,\n`Li₂ z = ∑_{k ≥ 0} z^(k+1)/(k+1)²`.\n\nIndexed from `k = 0` with numerator `z^(k+1)` so the `k`-th term is\n`z^(k+1)/(k+1)²`, matching `QOU.QPochhammer.LiTwo` term by term. Outside the\nclosed unit disc the `tsum` is `0` by Mathlib's junk-value convention; the\nlemmas below are all guarded by a disc hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0}]}